    {
      "title": "UK accuses Israeli ‘terrorists’ of ethnic cleansing in West Bank with government backing",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing",
      "description": "<p>In strongest condemnation ever by UK government, Ed Miliband announces sweeping sanctions on trade with Israeli settlements</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/08/uk-us-trade-israel-sanctions-labour-ed-miliband-farage-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Israeli “terrorists” are conducting ethnic cleansing in the West Bank with the tacit backing of the government, the UK foreign secretary, Ed Miliband has said, as he announced sweeping sanctions on trade with Israeli settlements.</p><p>In the strongest condemnation ever issued by the UK government, Miliband said the government would now take the official position that Israel’s occupation of the West Bank was unlawful in its entirety, saying such acknowledgment was “the least the people who face such suffering deserve. And it should be the prelude to justice.”</p><p>An import ban on goods from illegal settlements in the occupied territories.</p><p>A comprehensive sanctions regime against providing services such as construction or financing for Israeli settlements.</p><p>A ban on the advertising in the UK of illegal settlement properties.</p><p>Personal sanctions against key individuals accused of promoting settler violence.</p><p>A new ban for arms licences and other exports that “materially contribute to the occupation”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-08T14:45:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "Israel to close UK consulate in Jerusalem after sanctions against illegal settlements – UK politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/08/uk-us-trade-israel-sanctions-labour-ed-miliband-farage-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Foreign minister, Gideon Saar, claims UK ‘systemically working against the state of Israel’ as MPs including Jeremy Corbyn are also banned from country</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing\">UK accuses Israeli ‘terrorists’ of ethnic cleansing in West Bank with government backing</a></p></li></ul><p>The Liberal Democrats say they have been granted a Commons urgent question today about t<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/04/uk-ministers-hit-back-argentinian-falkland-islands-claim\">he latest Argentinian threats to the Falkland Islands</a>. A Foreign Office minister will be responding at about 12.30pm.</p><p><strong>Isaac Herzog</strong>, the Israeli president, has said that Britain will be “on the wrong side of history” if it goes ahead with plans to ban trade with the illegal settlements on the West Bank.</p><p>Later today, we expect to see headlines announcing certain British trade sanctions on Israeli settlements in Judea and Samaria.</p><p>If this happens – and other nations may join – I believe it will prove to be a grave miscalculation, a decision that will fall on the wrong side of history.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/08/uk-us-trade-israel-sanctions-labour-ed-miliband-farage-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-08T15:27:14"
    },
